[E-TEXT-PATTERN] Error: a text pattern can only take a fixed start
   ╭─[ reject/text-patterns-suffix.sw:5:5 ]
   │
 5 │   | name ++ ".sw" => True
   │     ──┬─  
   │       ╰─── only a text literal can stand before `++` in a pattern
   │ 
   │ Note: a pattern can match a text that starts a certain way, `"--" ++ rest`; to match one that ends a certain way or has a part in the middle, bind it to a variable and test it in a guard: `| t if t.endsWith ".sw" => …`, or take it apart with `Text.stripSuffix` or `Text.splitOn`
───╯
